note: The basic values, constants and f-strings, and how positions in text and lists are counted.
use DLC:string

number age = 25
str name = "Ann"
boolean active = true
list scores = [90, 85, 77]
map profile = {"name": "Ann", "city": "Seoul"}
constant number MAX_AGE = 120

print(name, age, active)
print(scores, profile)
print(f"{name} is {age}; the limit is {MAX_AGE}")

note: change gives an existing variable a new value.
age = age + 1
print(age)

note: Positions start at 1, a negative position counts from the end, and a~b includes both ends.
str city = "Seoul"
print(city[1], city[-1], city[2~4])
print(scores[1], scores[-1], scores[2~3])

note: Text is counted in characters, not bytes.
str hangul = "안녕하세요"
print(length(hangul), hangul[2~3], hangul[-1])

note: Arithmetic: / divides, % is the remainder, ** is a power, and ** binds tighter than a minus.
print(7 / 2, 7 % 3, 2 ** 10, -2 ** 2)

note: empty is the value of "nothing"; find gives it when the pattern is not there.
any digits = find("no digits here", p"[num]+")
print(digits is empty)
